# Public domain dedication (owner-confirmed 2026-09-18)

The repo-health reference implementation in this repository is dedicated to
the public domain. This is a port of the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal
summary into a plain-text dedication; for the full legal text see
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

## Dedication

The person(s) who created and contributed to this work hereby dedicate the
work to the public domain by waiving all of their rights to the work
worldwide under copyright law, including all related and neighboring rights,
to the extent allowed by law.

You may copy, modify, distribute, and perform the work, even for commercial
purposes, all without asking permission.

## Limitations

- In jurisdictions where a complete waiver is not possible, the work is
  licensed to you for any purpose without conditions, to the maximum extent
  permitted by law.
- Patent and trademark rights are not waived; contributors make no grant of
  patent rights by this dedication.
- The software is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind, express or
  implied. In no event shall contributors be liable for any claim arising
  from the use of this software.

## Note on third-party material

This dedication covers original repo-health sources in this repository. It
does not cover the sibling Elisa-compiler toolchain, vendored standard
libraries, or external data sources (forge APIs, advisory feeds, package
registries), each of which retains its own terms — see docs/THREAT_MODEL.md
and the per-source review register (M07-06) for details.
